<title>INDIA: Haque is new IDBI chief general manager.</title>
<headline>Haque is new IDBI chief general manager.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>M.M. Haque has taken over as chief general manager of Industrial Development Bank of India (IDBI), India's largest term-lending bank, a bank spokesman told Reuters on Monday.</p>
<p>Haque, 54, was general manager at IDBI in New Delhi until recently. He joined IDBI in 1979, having begun his career as a lecturer at Patna University and later serving with the Reserve Bank of India, India's central bank.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
